/*! \page module_java Java Rules

The Java module contains special build rules to create Java applications and modules.

The first step when using the <tt>java</tt> module is to include it.

\code
    IncludeModule java ;
\endcode

A simple example follows showing the process for building <tt>dlib.jar</tt> for a Defold build.

\code
    C.ActiveTarget dlib-java ;
    Java.SourcePaths : src/java ;
    Java.OutputPath : $(DYNAMO_HOME)/share/java ;
    Java.OutputName : dlib ;
    Java.Library :
        com/dynamo/crypt/Crypt.java
        com/dynamo/upnp/DeviceInfo.java
        com/dynamo/upnp/ISSDP.java
        com/dynamo/upnp/Request.java
        com/dynamo/upnp/Response.java
        com/dynamo/upnp/SSDP.java
    ;
\endcode

Note: This documentation came from the Android Rules. It is not fully up to date yet.


\section module_java_ruleslist List of Rules

