\refitem rule_Java_UncompressedAssetExtensions Java.UncompressedAssetExtensions
\endsecreflist

\section module_java_rules Rules

<hr>
\section rule_Java_Application rule Java.Application TARGET : SOURCES
\addindex rule_Java_Application

Compiles \c SOURCES and links them into \c TARGET.

\param TARGET The target to link \c SOURCES into.  The target name is given without extension.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param SOURCES The list of <tt>.java</tt> to link into the application.  Object and compiled Windows resource files may also be passed with this list.

\code
    Java.Application sdltest :
        org/libsdl/app/SDLActivity.java
        org/jamplus/sdltest/sdltestActivity.java
    ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_Assets rule Java.Assets TARGET : DIRECTORY
\addindex rule_Java_Assets

An Android application may contain user assets. The \c Java.Assets rule allows specification of the directory to be recursed and stored within the Android .apk application package.

Call \c Java.Assets before calling \c android.Package.

\param TARGET The target to attach the assets directory to.
\param DIRECTORY The base directory to use for the assets. There can only be one directory specified.

\code
    # Store all files and directories found by recursing c:/mygame/all_of_the_assets
    # within the Android package.
    Java.Assets : c:/mygame/all_of_the_assets ;
\endcode






<hr>
\section rule_Java_JarDirectories rule Java.JarDirectories TARGET : DIRECTORIES
\addindex rule_Java_JarDirectories

Specify paths to search when locating prebuilt JARs during the \c Java.Library and \c android.Package rule calls.

\param TARGET The target to apply the JAR search \c DIRECTORIES to. \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.  If \c TARGET is <tt>*</tt>, the directories are applied to every target needing them.
\param DIRECTORIES The list of directories to use when searching for JAR files. If relative directories are specified, they are rooted against the current \ref rule_SubDir.

\code
    # Search for extra prebuilt JARs within the $(SUBDIR)/libs directory.
    Java.JarDirectories : libs ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_Library rule Java.Library TARGET : SOURCES : OPTIONS
\addindex rule_Java_Library

\c Java.Library takes a list of Java \c SOURCES and builds a Java library out of them. It takes into account the following:

\htmlonly <blockquote> \endhtmlonly
<ul>
  <li>Any directories given for .jar searching via \ref rule_Java_JarDirectories.
  <li>Any prebuilt .jar files listed via \ref rule_Java_PrebuiltJars.
  <li>Any prebuilt .aar files listed via \ref rule_Java_PrebuiltAars. Any \c AndroidManifest.xml files within the .aar files are merged into a final \c AndroidManifest.xml for \ref rule_android_Package.
  <li>The search paths for .java files specified with \ref rule_Java_SourcePaths.
  <li>An \c AndroidManifest.xml for the target whose target name is given with \ref rule_Java_Manifest.
  <li>A package name given with \ref rule_Java_Package or automatically derived from the target's \c AndroidManifest.xml.
  <li>An assets directory given via \ref rule_Java_Assets.
  <li>A resources directory given by \ref rule_Java_Resources.
</ul>
\htmlonly </blockquote> \endhtmlonly

Dependencies are automatically derived, where possible, by looking at the contents of the <tt>.java</tt> files.

The resulting file is a .jar file.

\param TARGET The target to assign the \c FLAGS to.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param SOURCES The list of <tt>.java</tt> and <tt>.aidl</tt> files to build into a <tt>.jar</tt>.
\param OPTIONS Unused (except that \ref rule_Java_Application just calls \c Java.Library with \c OPTIONS of \c application).

\code
    Java.Library MyGame :
        the.java
        list.java
        of.java
        files.java
    ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_LinkJars rule Java.LinkJars TARGET : LIBRARIES
\addindex rule_Java_LinkJars

Makes \c TARGET depend on Jam-generated <tt>.jar</tt> \c LIBRARIES and uses them during linking.

\param TARGET The target to link \c LIBRARIES to.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param LIBRARIES The list of libraries to apply.  These libraries are those generated from the \ref rule_Java_Library rule.  They do not include prebuilt libraries.  To link prebuilt libraries, use the \ref rule_android_PrebuiltJars rule.

\code
    Java.LinkJars MyGame : MyLibrary ;
\endcode






<hr>
\section rule_Java_Manifest rule Java.Manifest TARGET : MANIFEST
\addindex rule_Java_Manifest

Assigns \c MANIFEST to be the "AndroidManifest.xml" file for this \c TARGET.

This rule is unneeded if \c MANIFEST is just an <tt>AndroidManifest.xml</tt> file found within <tt>\$(SUBDIR)</tt>.

\param TARGET The target to assign the \c MANIFEST to.
\param MANIFEST The target name of the <tt>AndroidManifest.xml</tt>.

\code
    # Use an AndroidManifest.xml within $(SUBDIR).
    Java.Manifest MyGame : AndroidManifest.xml ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_NativeLibraries rule Java.NativeLibraries TARGET : NATIVE_LIBRARIES
\addindex rule_Java_NativeLibraries

Makes \c TARGET depend on Jam-generated \c NATIVE_LIBRARIES. These are packaged during the \ref rule_Java_Package process.

\param TARGET The target to package the \c NATIVE_LIBRARIES into.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param NATIVE_LIBRARIES The list of libraries to apply.  These are shared libraries are those generated from the \ref rule_C_Library rule.  They do not include prebuilt libraries.  To package native prebuilt libraries, use the \ref rule_Java_NativePrebuiltLibraries rule.

\code
    C.Library MyNativeLibrary : blah.cpp : shared ;
    Java.NativeLibraries MyGame : MyNativeLibrary ;
    Java.Package ;
\endcode






<hr>
\section rule_Java_NativePrebuiltLibraries rule Java.NativePrebuiltLibraries TARGET : NATIVE_PREBUILT_LIBRARIES
\addindex rule_Java_NativePrebuiltLibraries

Makes \c TARGET depend on preexisting shared \c NATIVE_PREBUILT_LIBRARIES. These are packaged during the \ref rule_Java_Package process.

\param TARGET The target to package the \c NATIVE_PREBUILT_LIBRARIES into.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param NATIVE_PREBUILT_LIBRARIES The list of native prebuilt shared libraries to apply.  These libraries are shared libraries existing somewhere in the filesystem and are specified without an extension and without the leading 'lib' prefix.  For shared libraries generated from the \ref rule_C_Library rule, use the \ref rule_Java_NativeLibraries rule.

\code
    # Packages libmain.so into the MyGame.apk.
    Java.NativePrebuiltLibraries MyGame : main ;
    Java.Package ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_NativePrebuiltLibraryDirectories rule Java.NativePrebuiltLibraryDirectories TARGET : DIRECTORIES
\addindex rule_Java_NativePrebuiltLibraryDirectories

For the given \c TARGET, search \c DIRECTORIES for any libraries requested via \ref rule_Java_NativeLibraries. This rule must be called before \ref rule_android_Package.

Native libraries are searched for the following order:

\htmlonly <blockquote> \endhtmlonly
<ul>
  <li>Whatever \c SEARCH directories the user added.
  <li>The directories given through \c DIRECTORIES with an architecture appended. Current architectures are \c arm, \c armeabi-v7a, and \c x86.
</ul>
\htmlonly </blockquote> \endhtmlonly

\param TARGET The target to assign the native prebuilt library search \c DIRECTORIES to.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.  If \c TARGET is <tt>*</tt>, the defines are made available globally.
\param DIRECTORIES The list of directories to apply.  Absolute paths are used directly.  Relative paths are local to <tt>\$(SUBDIR)</tt>.  That is, they are relative to the subdirectory specified via \ref rule_SubDir "SubDir".

\code
    # Search for libmain.so in the current directory and in c:/some/directory/[architecture].
    Java.NativePrebuiltLibraryDirectories MyGame : c:/some/directory ;
    Java.NativePrebuiltLibraries MyGame : main ;
    Java.Package ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_Package rule Java.Package TARGET [ : TOOLCHAINS [ : OPTIONS ] ]
\addindex rule_Java_Package

In order to output a final .apk to be installed on an Android device, the \c Java.Package rule must be called. If \c TOOLCHAINS is specified, those requested toolchain components are packaged into the .apk. The passed in \c OPTIONS include additional build instructions such as automatic installation on a USB-connected Android device.

\c Java.Package should be the last rule called in a sequence of rule calls describing the build of an Android application.

\param TARGET The target to build.
\param TOOLCHAINS (optional) The list of toolchains used to build multiple architectures for the package. The default toolchain is used if none are specified.
\param OPTIONS The list of options applied when building the package.

\htmlonly <blockquote> \endhtmlonly
<ul>
  <li>\c install - Installs the .apk on the USB-connected Android device.
</ul>
\htmlonly </blockquote> \endhtmlonly

\code
    # Build a package for the current target using the active toolchain.
    Java.Package ;

    # Build a package for the target MyGame using the active toolchain.
    Java.Package MyGame ;

    # Build a package for the target MyGame using the active toolchain and install it to the USB-connected Android device.
    Java.Package MyGame : : install ;
\endcode






<hr>
\section rule_Java_PackageName rule Java.PackageName TARGET : PACKAGE_NAME
\addindex rule_Java_PackageName

Specify the package name for \c TARGET, generally in the form of <tt>com.module.submodule</tt>.

By default, this is read from the AndroidManifest.xml, so only call this if an override is needed.

\param TARGET The target to assign the link \c FLAGS to. \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param PACKAGE_NAME The package name to use.

\code
    Java.PackageName MyGame : com.mycompany.mygame ;
    Java.Package
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_PackageOutputPath rule Java.PackageOutputPath TARGET : PACKAGE_OUTPUT_PATH
\addindex rule_Java_PackageOutputPath

Assigns the location to output the final .apk to. This rule must be called prior to \c Java.Package.

\param TARGET The target to build.
\param PACKAGE_OUTPUT_PATH The directory to output the final .apk to. If a relative path is provided, that path is rooted against <tt>\$(SUBDIR)</tt>.

\code
    Java.PackageOutputPath MyGame : package ;
    Java.Package ;
\endcode






<hr>
\section rule_Java_PrebuiltAars rule Java.PrebuiltAars TARGET : LIBRARIES
\addindex rule_Java_PrebuiltAars

List out <tt>.aar</tt> files that \c Java.Library or \c android.Application need to link against. Makes \c TARGET depend on these preexisting <tt>.aar</tt> files.

By default, <tt>.aar</tt> files are searched for in <tt>\$(SUBDIR)/libs</tt>.

\param TARGET The target to link the \c LIBRARIES into.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param LIBRARIES The list of preexisting <tt>.aar</tt> files to use as part of the build, specified without the <tt>.aar</tt> extension.

\code
    Java.PrebuiltAars :
            appcompat-v7-23.1.1
            internalexternalpaths
            play-services-base-8.3.0
            play-services-basement-8.3.0
            play-services-drive-8.3.0
            play-services-games-8.3.0
            play-services-nearby-8.3.0
            play-services-plus-8.3.0
            support-v4-23.1.1
            unityads-release
    ;
\endcode








<hr>
\section rule_Java_PrebuiltJars rule Java.PrebuiltJars TARGET : LIBRARIES
\addindex rule_Java_PrebuiltJars

List out the <tt>.jar</tt> files that \c Java.Library or \c android.Application need to link against. Makes \c TARGET depend on these preexisting <tt>.jar</tt> files.

The \c LIBRARIES specified are, by default, searched for in <tt>\$(SUBDIR)</tt>.

\param TARGET The target to link the \c LIBRARIES into.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param LIBRARIES The list of preexisting <tt>.jar</tt> files to use as part of the build, specified without the <tt>.jar</tt> extension.

\code
    Java.PrebuiltJars :
            AndroidStore
            AndroidStoreAmazon
            in-app-purchasing-2.0.61
            SoomlaAndroidCore
            square-otto-1.3.2
            unity-classes
            UnityAndroidStore
            UnitySoomlaAndroidCore
    ;
\endcode








<hr>
\section rule_Java_ProductVersion rule Java.ProductVersion TARGET : VERSION_NAME : VERSION_CODE
\addindex rule_Java_ProductVersion

Sets the <tt>Java.versionName</tt> and <tt>android.versionCode</tt> properties in a <tt>build.gradle</tt> file.

\param VERSION_NAME The version name to be put into the <tt>AndroidManifest.xml</tt>'s <tt>android:versionName</tt>.
\param VERSION_CODE The version code to be put into the <tt>AndroidManifest.xml</tt>'s <tt>android:versionCode</tt>.

\code
    Java.ProductVersion THE_TARGET : 1.0 : 5 ;
\endcode









<hr>
\section rule_Java_Resources rule Java.Resources TARGET : DIRECTORIES
\addindex rule_Java_Resources

Sets \c DIRECTORIES as the locations to search for Android resources at when \c TARGET is built.

\param TARGET The target to which the resource search \c DIRECTORIES should be applied.  If not specified, \c TARGET defaults to the active target set via \ref rule_ActiveTarget "ActiveTarget".
\param DIRECTORIES The list of directories to search for resources. Relative directories are rooted against <tt>\$(SUBDIR)</tt>.

\code
    Java.Resources :
            ../unity-android-resources/res
            res
    ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_SDK rule Java.SDK SDK_VERSION : ARCHITECTURE
\addindex rule_Java_SDK

Sets the Android \c SDK_VERSION and \c ARCHITECTURE for the toolchain. Call this before any other <tt>Java.*</tt> rules.

\c Java.SDK attempts detection number of Android-specific tools and SDKs:

\htmlonly <blockquote> \endhtmlonly
<ul>
  <li>If the variable \c NDKROOT is not specified, the location of the Android NDK is searched for in an OS-dependent fashion.
    <ul>
        <li>On Windows, <tt>c:/Program Files (x86)/Android</tt> and then <tt>c:/</tt> is searched for a directory named <tt>android-ndk</tt> and a couple versioned derivatives.
    </ul>
  <li>Afterward, <tt>C.ARCHITECTURE</tt> is evaluated, and various compilation and linker flags are setup for use with the NDK.
  <li>Next, <tt>C.COMPILER</tt> is evaluated, and an NDK compiler toolchain is selected based on whether <tt>C.COMPILER</tt> is set to \c gcc or \c clang.
  <li>The Android SDK is detected next. If \c ANDROID_SDK_ROOT is set to a path, that path is assumed to be the root of the Android SDK toolchain. Otherwise, an OS-dependent default is chosen:
    <ul>
        <li>On Windows, <tt>c:/Program Files (x86)/Android/android-sdk</tt> is assumed to contain a properly installed Android SDK.
    </ul>
</ul>
\htmlonly </blockquote> \endhtmlonly

\param SDK_VERSION Defaults to \c 19.
\param ARCHITECTURE Defaults to <tt>armv7-a</tt>.

\code
    Java.SDK 19 : armv7-a ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_SDKCompileVersion rule Java.SDKCompileVersion TARGET : SDK_COMPILE_VERSION
\addindex rule_Java_SDKCompileVersion

Sets the Android \c SDK_COMPILE_VERSION to build against. Corresponds to the <tt>Java.compileSdkVersion</tt> property in a <tt>build.gradle</tt> file.

\param SDK_COMPILE_VERSION Defaults to the version specified by \ref rule_Java_SDK.

\code
    Java.SDKCompileVersion THE_TARGET : 30 ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_SDKMinimumVersion rule Java.SDKMinimumVersion TARGET : SDK_MINIMUM_VERSION
\addindex rule_Java_SDKMinimumVersion

Sets the Android \c SDK_MINIMUM_VERSION to ensure a build against. Corresponds to the <tt>Java.minSdkVersion</tt> property in a <tt>build.gradle</tt> file.

\param SDK_MINIMUM_VERSION Defaults to the version specified by \ref rule_Java_SDK.

\code
    Java.SDKMinimumVersion THE_TARGET : 24 ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_Sign rule Java.Sign TARGET : KEYSTORE_PATH_PASSWORD_KEY
\addindex rule_Java_Sign

Sets up the keystore information for the Android package. \c Java.Sign must be called before \c android.Package.

\param TARGET The target to sign.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param KEYSTORE_PATH_PASSWORD_KEY This parameter contains 4 entries, the path to the keystore, the password of the keystore, the key to use when accessing the keystore, and the password.

\code
    Java.Sign : $(SUBDIR)/my-keystore.keystore keystorepassword keyalias keypassword ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_SourcePaths rule Java.SourcePaths TARGET : DIRECTORIES
\addindex android_SourcePaths

Specify the source path for the Java files being built by \c TARGET. \c Java.SourcePaths must be called before \c android.Application or \c android.Library.

\param TARGET The target to assign the Java search path \c DIRECTORIES to.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param DIRECTORIES The list of directories to scan to find <tt>.java</tt> files. A given directory may either be absolute or relative. If relative, it is assumed to be based off of <tt>\$(SUBDIR)</tt>.

\code
    # Find com/mycompany/mylibrary/file.java at $(SUBDIR)/org/com/mycompany/mylibrary/file.java.
    Java.SourcePaths MyGame : org ;
\endcode







<hr>
\section rule_Java_UncompressedAssetExtensions rule Java.UncompressedAssetExtensions TARGET : UNCOMPRESSED_ASSET_EXTENSIONS
\addindex android_UncompressedAssetExtensions

Specify extensions to leave uncompressed when building the .apk. This must be called before \c Java.Package.

\param TARGET The target to leave the uncompressed file entries within.  \c TARGET is optional if \ref rule_ActiveTarget has been specified.
\param UNCOMPRESSED_ASSET_EXTENSIONS The list of extensions to leave uncompressed. Do not include a period in front of the extension.

\code
    # Leave .zip and .dat files uncompressed.
    Java.UncompressedAssetExtensions MyGame : zip dat ;
\endcode







<hr>
*/

